  "music": "w3-big-tent-bother",
  "authorNotes": "Solo, three checkpointed segments escalating the trampoline/trapeze interaction World 3 has been teaching since 01/02. Segment 1: trampoline-esc-1's springboard bounce is caught mid-air by trapeze-esc-1 (pivot 800,540, 300px bar) rather than landing on solid ground — the escalation is that the trampoline no longer aims you at a platform, it aims you at a grab. Segment 2 repeats the same trampoline-then-trapeze shape at a bigger gap and a lower damping (trapeze-esc-2, pivot 1750,480, 340px bar, 0.1 damping) so the margin for a late grab is smaller. Segment 3 flips the order — trapeze-esc-3 (pivot 2600,480, flush with pier C's own edge, the usual convention) swings out over open air and releases onto trampoline-esc-mid, a standalone landing pad with nothing under it but its own body, which bounces the short remaining hop up onto the goal pier. pose-w3-06 sits on pier C (tolerance 45) for players who want to strike a tightrope pose between segments 2 and 3 before committing to the flip. All three gaps carry an assist beam at the usual Clock cost."
